## ES Module Setup (Fixing `SyntaxError: Unexpected token 'export'`)

By default, Node.js treats `.js` files as CommonJS, while TypeScript compiles using ES module syntax (`export`). 

**Fix:**
Add `"type": "module"` to your `package.json` file so Node.js recognizes ES modules:

```json
{
  "name": "typescript",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "main": "app.js",
  "type": "module"
}
```

**Run the project:**
```bash
tsc
node app.js
```
